/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/rogue_use_magic_device_l13/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"rogue_use_magic_device_l13","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_trait (ClassFeatureMechanics family)","justification":"Use Magic Device grants three always-on benefits with no activation cost, no use count, and no rest reset cadence. The only existing ClassFeatureMechanics family ('activation') mandates activationCost, resource, and resetCadence. A passive_trait family is required to represent always-on class feature benefits that trigger automatically or are unconditionally active.","evidence":"You've learned how to maximize use of magic items, granting you the following benefits. — no activation trigger, no uses per rest, no cost stated anywhere in the feature."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"modify_attunement_cap","justification":"The Attunement benefit extends the character's attunement slot count from 3 to 4. No existing ClassFeatureEffect or v4 effect atom covers a numeric change to the attunement capacity. The v4 atom 'attunement_slot' is a consumed resource, not a cap modifier.","evidence":"You can attune to up to four magic items at once."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"charge_refund_on_roll","justification":"The Charges benefit introduces a stochastic 'roll 1d6, on 6 do not expend charges' mechanic triggered on each magic item charge expenditure. v4 has 'refund' as a procedure atom but no surface shape for a probabilistic die-gated charge refund. This is mechanically distinct from any existing effect, window, or resource atom — it requires a die-roll gate concept with no current representation.","evidence":"Whenever you use a magic item property that expends charges, roll 1d6. On a roll of 6, you use the property without expending the charges."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_scroll_access","justification":"The Scrolls benefit unlocks use of any Spell Scroll with Intelligence as spellcasting ability, plus a level-scaled DC ability check for higher-level scrolls (DC 10 + spell level) and item destruction on failure. v4 has 'grant_spell_access' for class spell list expansion, but no atom covers 'use a physical magic item (scroll) as a spell source with a custom casting ability, gated on a level-dependent ability check, with item destruction on failure'.","evidence":"You can use any Spell Scroll, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability... If the scroll contains a higher-level spell, you must first succeed on an Intelligence (Arcana) check (DC 10 plus the spell's level). On a failed check, the scroll disintegrates."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/rogue_use_magic_device_l13.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
