/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/sorcerer_spellcasting_l1/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"sorcerer_spellcasting_l1","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_grant (ClassFeature family)","justification":"Spellcasting is not activated — it permanently grants a spell slot pool and spell list access with no activation cost, no use-count, and no explicit reset cadence tied to the feature itself. The existing activation family mandates activationCost + UseCountResource + resetCadence, none of which model a spellcasting framework feature. A new family (e.g. passive_grant or spellcasting_framework) is needed for class features that are always-on grants of resources and access.","evidence":"Drawing from your innate magic, you can cast spells. [...] You know four Sorcerer cantrips of your choice. [...] The Sorcerer Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"grant_spell_access (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"The v4 taxonomy lists grant_spell_access as an effect atom, but it does not appear in the ClassFeatureEffect union type (which only contains GrantExtraActionEffect and HealHpEffect). Spellcasting grants cantrip and prepared-spell list access scaling by class level — this needs a ClassFeatureEffect variant that models the list source (class spell list), the initial known/prepared count, and the scaling schedule (threshold_tiers or linear_per_level with axis=class).","evidence":"You know four Sorcerer cantrips of your choice. [...] choose two level 1 Sorcerer spells. [...] The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Sorcerer levels."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"grant_spell_slot_pool (ClassFeatureEffect variant or resource shape)","justification":"The spell_slot resource atom exists in v4, but there is no surface type that models a class feature granting a full leveled slot table (e.g. 2 L1 slots at sorcerer L1, growing per class progression). This is distinct from a simple use_count: slots are differentiated by level, upcast constraints apply, and the reset is long-rest only. A new ClassFeatureEffect or resource shape is needed to express: class, axis=class, slot levels and counts per class level, resetCadence=long_rest.","evidence":"The Sorcerer Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"set_spellcasting_ability (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"Charisma is designated as the spellcasting ability, which determines spell attack rolls and save DCs for all sorcerer spells. This is a deterministic, class-feature-granted runtime fact (not DM adjudication), but it maps to no existing ClassFeatureEffect variant. It could be modeled as a modify_roll_substitute-like designation or a dedicated set_spellcasting_ability variant. Per ARCHITECTURE.md this may ultimately be pre-runtime character state, but at minimum the surface needs a way to record the designation.","evidence":"Charisma is your spellcasting ability for your Sorcerer spells."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/sorcerer_spellcasting_l1.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
