/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/mirror_image/proposal.md:81:- **New resolution type**: 1 (`probabilistic_gate`)
/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/mirror_image/proposal.md:84:This is a moderately sized surface expansion. The `on_incoming_hit_window` is likely reusable (Blur, Displacement-style effects also use defender-side incoming-hit windows). The `probabilistic_gate` is narrower but may apply to a small set of probabilistic defenses.
/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/mirror_image/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"mirror_image","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_hit_intercept","justification":"Mirror Image creates a persistent passive trigger that fires automatically when the caster is hit by an attack roll — no reaction cost, no player prompt, no Prepare/Prompt/Commit chain. This is structurally distinct from triggered_reaction (which requires a reaction-slot cast and the decision chain) and from ongoing_effect (whose operations are roll_modifier and damage_on_hit). The spell plants a 'on_incoming_hit_window' that resolves before damage is applied, gated by a probabilistic die check, consuming one token from a countable pool.","evidence":"Each time a creature hits you with an attack roll during the spell's duration, roll a d6 for each of your remaining duplicates."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"duplicate_pool resource","justification":"The spell creates exactly 3 destroyable tokens (duplicates) that serve as an ablative HP-like pool for the spell's interception mechanism. This is not use_count (which tracks activations of a feature), not spell_slot (consumed at cast), and not charge (charge items have a maximum and recharge). A duplicate_pool is a fixed-count token set that depletes as each token is destroyed by the interception mechanic.","evidence":"Three illusory duplicates of yourself appear in your space. [...] one of the duplicates is hit instead of you, and the duplicate is destroyed. The spell ends when all three duplicates are destroyed."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"on_incoming_hit_window","justification":"Mirror Image fires before the hit resolves — between the attacker rolling a hit and damage being applied. The existing on_hit_window fires after a hit is confirmed (attacker-side, grants a rider). Mirror Image needs an incoming-hit window on the defender side, which opens automatically (no action cost) and can negate the hit entirely by redirecting it. This is distinct from on_hit_window and from reaction_window (no reaction slot consumed).","evidence":"Each time a creature hits you with an attack roll during the spell's duration, roll a d6 for each of your remaining duplicates. If any of the d6s rolls a 3 or higher, one of the duplicates is hit instead of you."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"probabilistic_gate resolution","justification":"The interception check is 'roll Nd6, succeed if any die >= 3' where N = remaining duplicate count. This is neither an attack_roll, save_gate, nor ability_check. It is a pool-size-dependent probabilistic check with a fixed threshold. The surface has no resolution type for multi-die threshold checks.","evidence":"roll a d6 for each of your remaining duplicates. If any of the d6s rolls a 3 or higher, one of the duplicates is hit instead of you"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"intercept_hit","justification":"The successful resolution redirects the hit from the caster to a duplicate (destroying the duplicate). v4 has block_targeting (prevents being targeted before a roll) and grant_resistance (halves damage). Neither covers 'hit is retroactively redirected to a proxy token that is then destroyed'. This is a distinct deterministic effect: the caster takes no damage and no effects from the hit; the hit resolves against and destroys the duplicate.","evidence":"one of the duplicates is hit instead of you, and the duplicate is destroyed. The duplicates otherwise ignore all other damage and effects."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/mirror_image.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
