/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/divination/proposal.md:28:The 25% cumulative failure chance on repeated castings within a Long Rest introduces a probabilistic gate: roll dice to determine whether the DM gives any answer at all. The gate is mechanically trivial (a single d100 < threshold check), but even when the gate passes, the _content_ of the answer is DM-decided. The failure branch yields "no information," which is not a creature-state change.
/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/divination/proposal.md:30:Neither half of this secondary mechanic forces a new atom or family — the probabilistic check is caller-resolved and the outcome is narrative in both branches.
/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/results-srd/divination/result.json:8:  "notes": "The entire mechanical payload of Divination is DM adjudication: the caster asks a question about a specific goal, event, or activity within 7 days, and the DM offers a truthful reply. No deterministic mechanical resolution exists — no attack roll, saving throw, damage, heal, condition, or creature-state change. The secondary mechanic (cumulative 25% failure chance on repeated castings before a Long Rest) is a probabilistic gate before the DM response, but the content of the answer remains caller-owned narrative. Both mechanics are DM-agenda and outside core per ARCHITECTURE.md."
